    <item>
      <title>Generalized Riemann Hypothesis proof in Lean 4, in 76k lines (down from 17M)</title>
      <link>https://leanprover.zulipchat.com/#narrow/channel/658556-Riemann-Hypothesis/topic/Cleaning.20up.20the.20proof/near/643702366</link>
      <guid>https://lobste.rs/s/tlwot6</guid>
      <author>leanprover.zulipchat.com via mikedanese</author>
      <pubDate>Wed, 25 Nov 2026 16:26:56 -0600</pubDate>
      <comments>https://lobste.rs/s/tlwot6/generalized_riemann_hypothesis_proof</comments>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;This is a shortened version of Alpöge's Lean proof of RH and GRH for Dirichlet L-functions (&lt;a href="https://alpo.ge/remark.pdf" rel="ugc"&gt;https://alpo.ge/remark.pdf&lt;/a&gt;), which was about 17 million lines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;There are two editions proving the same five theorems: a readable one at about 300,000 lines (start at grh/GUIDE.md) and a compact one at about 76,000.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Github repo: &lt;a href="https://github.com/lsernau/grh-lean" rel="ugc"&gt;https://github.com/lsernau/grh-lean&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://lobste.rs/s/tlwot6/generalized_riemann_hypothesis_proof"&gt;Comments&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      <category>math</category>
    </item>
